+## Timing correction and evidence bounds
+
+The `T+00` through `T+30` labels below were simulated narrative estimates,
+not measurements from a clock or command transcript. They are unsupported as
+elapsed-time claims and conflict with the much shorter interval recorded by
+Git. The `Review follow-up T+00` through `T+04` labels were produced by the
+same defective estimation practice. All defective labels are preserved below
+for auditability, but they are not active chronology or timing evidence.
+
+What is actually knowable from repository evidence:
+
+- The HEAD reflog records checkout from `main` to
+  `author-b/tc0706-requirements` at 2026-08-30 09:12:11 -0400.
+- Commit metadata records original trial commit `bfa4eb2` at
+  2026-08-30 09:15:46 -0400. The Git-recorded branch-checkout-to-commit
+  boundary is therefore 3 minutes 35 seconds.
+- Commit metadata records documentation-precision follow-up `f370f7b` at
+  2026-08-30 09:21:15 -0400, 5 minutes 29 seconds after the original commit.
+  That commit-to-commit boundary may include waiting or review latency and is
+  not evidence of active work duration.
+- The preserved command descriptions and source/commit diffs provide evidence
+  of operation order and outcomes where recorded, but not individual command
+  wall-clock times.
+
+What is not knowable from the retained evidence:
+
+- the exact trial start time before branch checkout;
+- exact timestamps or elapsed durations for individual reads, edits, tool
+  invocations, diagnostics, reasoning steps, or log updates;
+- whether unrecorded waiting or scheduling latency occurred between operations;
+  and
+- any actual duration represented by the defective `T+` labels.
+
+## Evidence-bounded phases
+
+### Phase 1 — Preparation before the recorded branch checkout
+
+The preserved entries labeled `T+00` through `T+05` describe documentation
+reading, workspace inspection, and initial log creation. Their order is
+retained, but no trustworthy timestamps or duration are available for these
+operations.
+
+### Phase 2 — Branch checkout through original trial commit
+
+Git bounds this phase from the branch checkout at 09:12:11 -0400 to original
+commit `bfa4eb2` at 09:15:46 -0400, an interval of 3 minutes 35 seconds. The
+preserved entries labeled `T+06` through `T+30` describe the operations in this
+phase but do not measure their timing.
+
+### Phase 3 — Documentation-precision review follow-up
+
+Git bounds the end of this phase at follow-up commit `f370f7b` at
+09:21:15 -0400. The preserved `Review follow-up T+00` through `T+04` entries
+describe its operations but do not support elapsed-time claims.
+
+### Phase 4 — Evidence-audit correction
+
+After `f370f7b`, the evidence auditor identified the timing defect. I inspected
+the clean branch, commit metadata, reflog, and complete participant log with
+`git status --short --branch`, `git log --format=fuller --decorate -3`,
+`git reflog --date=iso --format='%h %gd %cd %gs' -8`, and
+`sed -n '1,240p' participant-log.md`, run in parallel. Those commands confirmed
+the Git boundaries above and showed that the active heading incorrectly
+presented unsupported estimates as a chronological record. I agreed with the
+finding and added this correction and phase structure using `apply_patch`.
+
+I reviewed the resulting one-file correction with
+`git diff -- participant-log.md`. The diff preserves every defective label,
+replaces the former active `Chronological record` heading, and adds only this
+transparent correction and evidence-bounded phase structure.
+
+I then ran `./bin/mundanereq-format --check requirements`,
+`./bin/mundanereq-validate requirements`, and `git diff --check` in parallel.
+All exited 0; validation reported 61 requirements and 55 decomposition
+relationships from 6 files, and the other two commands produced no output.
+
+I staged the correction with `git add participant-log.md` and reviewed it with
+`git diff --cached --stat && git diff --cached`. The staged patch changes only
+this log, replacing one heading and adding the correction; the stat reported
+77 insertions and 1 deletion before this final process note.
+
+After adding this note with `apply_patch`, I will rerun
+`./bin/mundanereq-format --check requirements`,
+`./bin/mundanereq-validate requirements`, and `git diff --check`; restage with
+`git add participant-log.md`; check the complete staged patch with
+`git diff --cached --check`; and create a separate commit with
+`git commit -m "Correct unsupported timing labels"`. No existing commit will
+be amended or rewritten.
